# Browser
# Bot1 casts Requiting Hex in the browser. The optional cost is offered with what it does ("Blight 1: put a -1/-1 counter on a creature
# you control") beside "Cast without blighting", under a title that says it is an additional cost; the creature to put the counter on is
# captioned "choose a creature you control to blight (it gets -1/-1 counters)", not "keep"; one creature on the battlefield answers on the click, with no button to confirm. Bot1's Ornithopter takes it, Bot2's Llanowar Elves is destroyed and Bot1 gains 2.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Ornithopter
Requiting Hex
Island x4
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Llanowar Elves
Island x5
Island x13

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Requiting Hex.Cast
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Title = Requiting Hex: choose an additional cost to pay
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Modes = Cast without blighting; Blight 1: put a -1/-1 counter on a creature you control
Bot1.Modes(Blight 1)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Title = Requiting Hex: choose a creature you control to blight (it gets -1/-1 counters)
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Detail = 0 of 1 chosen  ·  click them on the battlefield
Bot1.Choose(Pay mana)
Bot1.Choose(Ornithopter)
? Client.Bot1.Confirm =
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 22
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.MinusOneMinusOne = 1
Bot2.Graveyard = Llanowar Elves
